    "collection": "hr_policies",
    "summary": "Governed by Labour Law No. 8 of 1996, as amended to 2023.",
    "content": "Governed by **Labour Law No. 8 of 1996**, as amended to 2023.\n\n## Annual leave — Article 61\n- **14 days** per year.\n- **21 days** after five consecutive years with the same employer.\n- Official holidays, religious holidays and weekends are **excluded** from the count.\n- Carry-over is permitted to the following year only, and lapses after that.\n- Leave may be split, in blocks of not less than two days.\n\n## End of service — Article 32 and the Social Security Corporation\n**For a normal private-sector employee, no employer-paid gratuity is owed on leaving — whether you\nresign or are terminated.**\n\nArticle 32 provides one month wage per year of service, but it opens with a carve-out: it applies\nonly to a worker **not** subject to the Social Security Law. SSC coverage is compulsory for all\nworkers subject to the Labour Law aged 16 or over, regardless of contract type, at any employer with\none or more workers. The residual class is narrow — mainly irregular workers engaged fewer than 16\ndays a month.\n\nWhat you receive instead is your SSC entitlement: an old-age pension or lump-sum compensation, plus\nyour unemployment-insurance savings balance.\n\n## Arbitrary dismissal — Article 25\nIf a court finds within sixty days that a termination was arbitrary, it may order reinstatement or\ncompensation of **half a month wage per year of service, with a floor of two months wages**,\ncomputed on the last wage, in addition to notice allowance.\n\nThe \"three to six months\" figure still widely quoted is the **superseded** pre-2019 value, replaced\nby Law No. 14 of 2019.\n\n## Probation — Article 35\n**Three months** maximum, with no extension or renewal mechanism in the law at all. Termination\nduring probation requires no notice and pays no compensation. If you are kept on past probation the\ncontract becomes indefinite-term and the probation counts towards total service.\n\n## Sick leave — Article 65\n- **14 days** at full pay, on a report from a physician approved by the firm.\n- A further **14 days at full pay** where the worker is an inpatient.\n- There is **no reduced-pay tier** — both blocks are full pay, contrary to a common misconception.\n- In establishments of 20 or more workers the medical report must be approved by a medical committee.\n\n## ملخص\nالإجازة السنوية ١٤ يوماً وترتفع إلى ٢١ يوماً بعد خمس سنوات متصلة لدى صاحب العمل نفسه.\nولا يستحق الموظف المشمول بالضمان الاجتماعي بدل نهاية خدمة من صاحب العمل، إذ تنطبق المادة ٣٢ فقط على غير الخاضعين لقانون الضمان، والشمول إلزامي لجميع العاملين تقريباً.\nوفي حالة الفصل التعسفي تنص المادة ٢٥ على نصف أجر شهر عن كل سنة خدمة بحد أدنى أجر شهرين.\nفترة التجربة ثلاثة أشهر دون آلية تمديد. والإجازة المرضية ١٤ يوماً بأجر كامل يضاف إليها ١٤ يوماً بأجر كامل عند التنويم.",
    "searchText": "Employment Terms — Jordan \nEmployment Terms — Jordan \nشروط العمل — الأردن \nشروط العمل — الأردن \nJordan labour law, end of service Jordan, social security corporation, annual leave Jordan, probation Jordan \nقانون العمل الأردني, نهاية الخدمة الأردن, الضمان الاجتماعي, الإجازة السنوية, فترة التجربة \ncountry terms \nJO \nGoverned by **Labour Law No. 8 of 1996**, as amended to 2023.\n\n## Annual leave — Article 61\n- **14 days** per year.\n- **21 days** after five consecutive years with the same employer.\n- Official holidays, religious holidays and weekends are **excluded** from the count.\n- Carry-over is permitted to the following year only, and lapses after that.\n- Leave may be split, in blocks of not less than two days.\n\n## End of service — Article 32 and the Social Security Corporation\n**For a normal private-sector employee, no employer-paid gratuity is owed on leaving — whether you\nresign or are terminated.**\n\nArticle 32 provides one month wage per year of service, but it opens with a carve-out: it applies\nonly to a worker **not** subject to the Social Security Law. SSC coverage is compulsory for all\nworkers subject to the Labour Law aged 16 or over, regardless of contract type, at any employer with\none or more workers. The residual class is narrow — mainly irregular workers engaged fewer than 16\ndays a month.\n\nWhat you receive instead is your SSC entitlement: an old-age pension or lump-sum compensation, plus\nyour unemployment-insurance savings balance.\n\n## Arbitrary dismissal — Article 25\nIf a cou",
