    "title": "Annual Leave — Saudi Arabia",
    "titleAr": "الإجازة السنوية — السعودية",
    "category": "leave",
    "country": "SA",
    "version": "1.0",
    "owner": "HR Policy",
    "citation": "Saudi Labour Law, Article 109",
    "verified": true,
    "collection": "hr_policies",
    "summary": "Under Article 109 of the Saudi Labour Law:",
    "content": "## Entitlement\nUnder **Article 109 of the Saudi Labour Law**:\n\n- **21 days** per year for employees with less than five years of continuous service.\n- **30 days** per year once the employee completes **five continuous years** with the employer.\n\nThe step-up is based on continuous service with this employer. Service with a previous employer does\nnot count.\n\n## How it is counted\nCalendar days.\n\n## Practical points\n- The employer schedules leave according to business needs, but must let you take your entitlement.\n- Unused leave is paid on termination.\n- Ask the agent for your own balance rather than assuming: it reflects days already taken and any\n  request still awaiting approval.\n\n## الاستحقاق\nبموجب **المادة ١٠٩ من نظام العمل السعودي**:\n- **٢١ يوماً** سنوياً لمن تقل خدمته المتصلة عن خمس سنوات.\n- **٣٠ يوماً** سنوياً لمن أتم **خمس سنوات متصلة** لدى صاحب العمل.\n\nوتُحتسب بالأيام التقويمية، ويُدفع بدل الرصيد غير المستخدم عند انتهاء الخدمة.",
    "searchText": "Annual Leave — Saudi Arabia \nAnnual Leave — Saudi Arabia \nالإجازة السنوية — السعودية \nالإجازة السنوية — السعودية \nannual leave saudi, 21 days, 30 days, five years, vacation entitlement KSA \nإجازة سنوية السعودية, ٢١ يوم, ٣٠ يوم, خمس سنوات, استحقاق الإجازة \nleave \nSA \n## Entitlement\nUnder **Article 109 of the Saudi Labour Law**:\n\n- **21 days** per year for employees with less than five years of continuous service.\n- **30 days** per year once the employee completes **five continuous years** with the employer.\n\nThe step-up is based on continuous service with this employer. Service with a previous employer does\nnot count.\n\n## How it is counted\nCalendar days.\n\n## Practical points\n- The employer schedules leave according to business needs, but must let you take your entitlement.\n- Unused leave is paid on termination.\n- Ask the agent for your own balance rather than assuming: it reflects days already taken and any\n request still awaiting approval.\n\n## الاستحقاق\nبموجب **المادة ١٠٩ من نظام العمل السعودي**:\n- **٢١ يوماً** سنوياً لمن تقل خدمته المتصلة عن خمس سنوات.\n- **٣٠ يوماً** سنوياً لمن أتم **خمس سنوات متصلة** لدى صاحب العمل.\n\nوتُحتسب بالأيام التقويمية، ويُدفع بدل الرصيد غير المستخدم عند انتهاء الخدمة.",
